{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. The other data variables (`N`, `K`, and `x`) are context inputs used only for sizes and indexing/prediction. Parameters `mu` and `sigma` each have exactly one built-in prior before they are used in the likelihood.
","model_safe_stan":"// Comparison of k groups with common variance (ANOVA)
data {
  int<lower=0> N; // number of observations
  int<lower=0> K; // number of groups
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> x; // discrete group indicators
  vector[N] y; // real valued observations
}
parameters {
  vector[K] mu;        // group means
  real<lower=0> sigma; // common standard deviation constrained to be positive
}
model {
  mu ~ normal(0, 100); // weakly informative prior
  sigma ~ normal(0, 1); // weakly informative prior
  y ~ normal(mu[x], sigma); // observation model / likelihood
}
","data_safe_json":"{
  "K": 4,
  "N": 1,
  "x": [
    2
  ],
  "y": [
    1.0
  ]
}","protected_variables":["y"]}
